  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Take an initial pass at the implementation of the OCFLPersistentStorageSession.  The OCFLPersistentStorageSession is responsible for maintaining the association between a session id,  the fedora resource  and an OCFLSession which should operate on a single OCFL resource.  So for each OCFLPersistentStorageSession there are one or more open OCFLSession.  On commit,  the OCFLPersistentStorageSession loops through the ocfl sessions and commits each one.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
